<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tüsheet Khanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1580 CE – 1691 CE (approx.) · capital Erdene Zuu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The central and leading Khalkha khanate of Outer Mongolia, whose khans founded Erdene Zuu monastery and whose family produced the first Jebtsundamba Khutughtu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a> were given by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayan-khan">Dayan Khan</a> to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geresenje">Geresenje</a>, whose descendants divided them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abtai-sain-khan">Abtai</a>, a great-grandson of Dayan Khan, became the leading prince of central Khalkha, met the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonam-gyatso">Third Dalai Lama</a> in 1586 and received the title Khan; his successors took the title Tüsheet Khan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The khans ruled nomadic subjects along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-river">Orkhon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuul-river">Tuul</a> valleys through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghisid-principle">Chinggisid</a> nobles. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abtai-sain-khan">Abtai Khan</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdene-zuu">Erdene Zuu</a> monastery beside the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakorum">Karakorum</a> around 1585, a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug Buddhism</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanabazar">Zanabazar</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gombodorj">Tüsheet Khan Gombodorj</a>, became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebtsundamba-khutughtu">Jebtsundamba Khutughtu</a>, the head of Mongolian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, as well as a famous sculptor.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tüsheet Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakhundorj">Chikhundorj's</a> war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zasagt-khanate">Zasagt Khanate</a> in 1687 gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> ruler Galdan a pretext to invade; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha</a> refugees fled south, and in 1691 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dolon-nor">Dolon Nor</a> the Khalkha princes submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>, becoming a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing</a> province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1580 CE – 1691 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.14%;width:2.21%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1580 CE – 1691 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Erdene Zuu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abtai Sain Khan, Gombodorj, Chikhundorj</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tibetan Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khalkha Mongolian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tusheet Khan Aimag, Tushetu Khan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1636&amp;focus=tusheet-khanate" aria-label="Tüsheet Khanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7152 551 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tüsheet Khanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7817 927h0M7567 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7472 807h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7472 807h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mongolia. <a href="/atlas?year=1636&amp;focus=tusheet-khanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
